 "about_text": "Monte Vista Projects is a Los Angeles artist-run collective founded in 2007. Operating from a fifth-floor space on Maple Avenue downtown, it presents exhibitions, lectures, events, and performances that question standards set by academia and mainstream contemporary art institutions. The collective prioritizes under-represented artists and regularly partners with local, national, and international artist-run spaces, including collaborations and exchanges with groups in Rotterdam, Berlin, and across Southern California. Monte Vista Projects is run collectively by a rotating roster of member-artists who organize its programming, and it maintains an open internship and volunteer program supporting exhibitions, gallery hosting, and installation.",
